//ERR 14 3 14 6
//MSG="This function does not return a value in all control paths"

// The `for` counterpart of 81e_the_only_return_is_inside_a_while.cpl. `0..0` is
// an empty range — see 04_control_flow/11_for_over_an_empty_range.cpl — so the
// body never runs.
//
// A `for` reaches the check already lowered to `while $iter.has_next()`, so at
// the IR level this is not a second case at all. It is worth writing anyway: at
// the source level a reader has to be told that no `for` counts as returning
// whatever its bounds look like, and `has_next()` is the condition someone would
// be tempted to reason about if the exemption were ever widened past the literal
// `true`. The check stays structural instead.

fn f n
    for i 0..n
        ret i

fn main
    out "{f(0)}"
